module.exports = JSON.parse('{"aboutMe":{"image":"/aboutMe/profile-picture.jpg","imageBlur":"/aboutMe/profile-picture-blur.jpg","paraOne":"Hey, if you\'re a recruiter just scanning for keywords, I got you covered.","paraTwo":"When it comes to brainstorming, you\'ll find me using <b>Miro</b> to map out my ideas.\\nFor wireframing and design, I\'m a big fan of both <b>Adobe XD</b> and <b>Figma</b>.\\nWhen it\'s time to develop websites, I rely on <b>React</b> and its frameworks like NextJS.\\nI also have experience in developing mobile apps using <b>React Native</b>.\\nTo keep my thoughts organized , I use <b>NotesApp</b> (which I actually built myself!).\\nAnd of course, I collaborate with my team using tools like <b>Slack</b> and <b>Discord</b>.","paraThree":"For the rest of you: I\'m passionate about creating products that focus on user experience and performance. I love working on the front-end of things and collaborating with designers. That\'s how I discovered my love for wireframes and personas, and started my journey into the world of UI/UX.\\nI\'ve been lucky enough to work on a variety of UI/UX projects as both a developer and a designer. Having experience on both sides of the process helps me bridge the gap between teams and make the handover process smoother.\\nWhen I\'m not working, you can find me doing a few things. I love watching football, playing football, and even gaming (mostly football games, of course). I also like to tend to my garden, tinker with my PC (which I built myself!), and write for Plain English and Bootcamp.\\nAnd did I mention football? It\'s kind of my thing.","careerGraph":[{"name":"Moonraft Innovation Labs","date":"2017-2019"},{"name":"Piktorlabs India","date":"2019-2022"},{"name":"UST","date":"2023-Present"},{"name":"Maybe you?"}],"resumeLink":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1klz65Dy8oZEWaxDepYZymZRQCGSjI_AC/view?usp=sharing"},"landingPage":{"firstLine":"Good day to you!","links":[{"icon":"microsoft","title":"Microsoft","url":"mailto:abhisheknr21@outlook.com"},{"icon":"linkedin","title":"LinkedIn","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/6foot4/"},{"icon":"github","title":"github","url":"https://www.github.com/abhisheknairofficial"},{"icon":"quora","title":"quora","url":"https://www.quora.com/profile/Abhishek-Nair-147"},{"icon":"medium","title":"Medium","url":"https://medium.com/@abhisheknairp"},{"icon":"twitter","title":"Twitter","url":"https://twitter.com/nairgalactico21"}],"paraOne":"Hello, my name is Abhishek, and I\'m a developer based in Seattle, WA. With over 5 years of experience in the industry, I currently hold the position of Lead Software Engineer at UST.","paraTwo":"My strength lies in contributing to the user experience and frontend aspects of software development. I believe in constantly honing my skills in these areas to deliver exceptional products that meet needs and exceed expectations.","quote":"<YellowText>designer</YellowText> | front-end developer","title":"I\'m <B>Abhishek</B>"},"letsTalk":{"email":"abhisheknr4@gmail.com","paragraph":"If you want to chat about a freelance project, job opportunity, or even just learn more about how I created this site, don\'t hesitate to reach out to me below!","image":"/letsTalk/contact-image.svg"},"projectsPage":{"projects":[{"description":"Collaborating with a friend, I recently led the redesign and development if the IF magazine website. Working alongside a talented architect-turned-designer, I leveraged my interdisciplinary skills to bridge the gap between design and development and create a seamless user experience. Throughout the project, I utilized my expertise in both design and development to ensure that the website was not only visually stunning but also highly functional and user-friendly. By reducing the friction between the two disciplines, I was able to create a more efficient and streamlined development process. The opportunity to work on this project was incredibly rewarding, and I\'m proud of the impact that our team was able to make.","icon":"/projects/ifmag-logo.webp","image":"/projects/ifmag.webp","title":"Case Study: Redesigning the website for ‘The Intersectional Feminist’","client":"The Intersectional Feminist","tags":["research","visual design","development"],"url":"https://medium.muz.li/case-study-redesigning-the-website-for-the-intersectional-feminist-8a6c9900e675"},{"description":"n just 14 weeks, I designed and developed a mobile app for both iOS and Android platforms, from initial conception to final mockups. This project was the result of my UI/UX training at DesignBoat, where I gained expertise in the entire product life cycle. Throughout the project, I applied my skills in user research, information architecture, wireframing, prototyping, and visual design to create a seamless user experience that met our target audience\'s needs. The result is a stunning mobile app that showcases my ability to turn ideas into tangible products. I\'m committed to refining my UI/UX design skills and pursuing opportunities to create impactful solutions that enhance people\'s lives.","icon":"/projects/designboat.webp","image":"/projects/cleansneaker.webp","title":"From Concept to Reality: A Case Study on Developing a Specialized Sneaker Experience for Enthusiasts","client":"designboat","tags":["research","visual design"],"url":"https://bootcamp.uxdesign.cc/case-study-creating-a-specialised-experience-for-sneaker-heads-5cd00941eb78"},{"description":"When I started the 100-day UI challenge, I was a complete beginner to design tools and online resources. But through dedication and persistence, I gradually honed my skills and built up my knowledge base. As I completed each of the 100 problem statements, I gained a deeper understanding of the nuances of UI design, from typography and color theory to layout and user experience. By the time I finished the challenge, I had transformed from a novice to a skilled designer, with a wealth of knowledge at my fingertips. The experience was a true test of my durability and commitment, but it was also incredibly rewarding. I\'m excited to continue pushing myself and exploring new challenges as I build my career in UI design.","icon":"/projects/dribbble.svg","image":"/projects/daily-ui.webp","title":"100 Days of Growth: My Journey of Improving UI Skills Through a Daily Challenge","client":"Dribbble","tags":["ui design","daily challenge"],"url":"https://dribbble.com/AbhishekNairOfficial/collections/2732240-Daily-UI"}],"text":"Here\'s some of my work","title":"Projects:"},"devProjects":[{"description":"As part of my journey in learning UI/UX design, I took on the challenge of redesigning my own website from scratch. After completing the design and development phases, I realized that the deployment process was a bit cumbersome. At the time, the only way to deploy updates was to manually merge code into the master branch and then deploy using the command line interface (CLI). I began researching alternative deployment methods to simplify the process and make it more efficient.","icon":"/projects/plain-english.webp","image":"/projects/firebase-deploy.webp","title":"How to Host Your Own React Site: A Step-by-Step Guide Using Firebase and Github Actions","type":"development","tags":["javascript","reactjs","firebase"],"client":"JavaScript in plain English","buttonText":"Read the article here","url":"https://javascript.plainenglish.io/hosting-your-own-react-site-using-firebase-and-github-actions-8a518255cc64"},{"description":"As the WFH culture grew globally in 2020 due to the pandemic, I found myself with more time on my hands at home. I decided to put my skills to use and create a simple game. With so many people now spending time online, I thought it would be a fun way to provide some entertainment for others. With a focus on simplicity and user experience, I spent several weeks developing the game and refining it until I was happy with the final product. Overall, it was a fulfilling project that not only helped me improve my skills but also brought joy to others during a challenging time.","icon":"/projects/tic-tac-toe.svg","image":"/projects/tic-tac-toe.png","title":"Creating a Simple Game During the Rise of WFH Culture","client":"Hosted on Firebase","type":"development","buttonText":"Play the game here","tags":["javascript","reactjs","game design"],"url":"https://ttt-backend-42a99.web.app/"},{"description":"As a young developer, I was thrilled by the idea of creating something that could run on billions of devices. That\'s what inspired me to learn how to build mobile apps. Soon after, I set out to create a simple, yet useful application that I could use myself and share with others. And that\'s how NotesApp was born - a sleek and intuitive note-taking app designed to help users stay organized and productive on the go.","icon":"/projects/medium.svg","image":"/projects/NotesApp.webp","title":"From Dream to Reality: The Story of Creating NotesApp","client":"Medium","tags":["ui design","development","react native"],"url":"https://medium.com/@6foot4/notesapp-b443bb9b2ac9"}],"testimonials":[{"name":"The IF Mag team","role":"I helped redesign and develop their blog","message":"Would I recommend Abhishek to my friends? Definitely!  Abhishek is a complete package when it comes to design and development!"}],"socialProfiles":[{"icon":"behance","link":"https://www.behance.net/abhisheknairofficial"},{"icon":"linkedin","link":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/6foot4/"},{"icon":"medium","link":"https://medium.com/@6foot4"},{"icon":"dribbble","link":"https://dribbble.com/AbhishekNairOfficial"},{"icon":"github","link":"https://github.com/abhisheknairofficial"}]}');

